{"id":"brandenburg-gate","name":"Brandenburg Gate","qid":"Q82425","country":"Germany","locality":"Berlin, Bezirk Mitte","lat":"52.516272222","lon":"13.377722222","built":"1791","year":1791,"year_text":"1791","century":"18th century","era":"Early modern","period":"Kingdom of Prussia","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"Greek Revival architecture","heritage":"architectural heritage monument; cultural heritage monument in Berlin","type":"city gate; national symbol; triumphal arch; architectural landmark; border checkpoint","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandenburg_Gate","text":"The Brandenburg Gate (German: Brandenburger Tor [ˈbʁandn̩ˌbʊʁɡɐ ˈtoːɐ̯] ) is an 18th-century neoclassical monument in Berlin, Germany. One of the best-known landmarks of the country, it was erected on the site of a former city gate that marked the start of the road from Berlin to Brandenburg an der Havel, the former capital of the Margraviate of Brandenburg. The current structure was built from 1788 to 1791 by orders of King Frederick William II of Prussia, based on designs by the royal architect Carl Gotthard Langhans.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandenburg_Gate","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-159f65320a46","w":1200,"h":801,"title":"Brandenburg Gate (8331820462).jpg","o":"gh-159f65320a46.jpg","credit":{"text":"Steve Collis from Melbourne, Australia","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brandenburg_Gate_%288331820462%29.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-ae6d5e0af6f2","w":1200,"h":802,"title":"Brandenburger Tor morgens.jpg","o":"gh-ae6d5e0af6f2.jpg","credit":{"text":"Thomas Wolf , www.foto-tw.de","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brandenburger_Tor_morgens.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"empire-total-war--brandenbu